## PoC Generation Results — `Ap4HintTrackReader.h`

| # | Vulnerability | Status | Reason |
|---|---|---|---|
| 001 | OOB Read on empty `GetTrackIds()[0]` | **UNVERIFIED** | `mp42aac` never calls `AP4_HintTrackReader::Create()` |
| 002 | NULL Pointer Dereference via missing track ID | **UNVERIFIED** | same — unreachable code path from `mp42aac` |
| 003 | Integer Underflow in `WriteSampleRtpData` (`sample_num=0`) | **UNVERIFIED** | same — `nm` confirms `mp42aac` doesn't link the hint reader |

### Root cause of all three being UNVERIFIED

`mp42aac` only locates `TYPE_AUDIO` tracks and writes AAC samples. It never instantiates `AP4_HintTrackReader`, so all three vulnerabilities in `Ap4HintTrackReader.h` are **dead code paths** for this binary. The correct triggering binary would be `Mp4RtpHintInfo` (source at `Source/C++/Apps/Mp4RtpHintInfo/`), but it is not present in `build_test/bin/`.

